00034 {\cf20 //--------------------------------------------}\par
00035 {\cf20 // ABOUT THE MEANING OF THE 'static' KEYWORD:}\par
00036 {\cf20 //--------------------------------------------}\par
00037 {\cf20 // In this demo code, we frequently use 'static' variables inside functions.}\par
00038 {\cf20 // A static variable persists across calls. It is essentially a global variable but declared inside the scope of the function.}\par
00039 {\cf20 // Think of "static int n = 0;" as "global int n = 0;" !}\par
00040 {\cf20 // We do this IN THE DEMO because we want:}\par
00041 {\cf20 // - to gather code and data in the same place.}\par
00042 {\cf20 // - to make the demo source code faster to read, faster to change, smaller in size.}\par
00043 {\cf20 // - it is also a convenient way of storing simple UI related information as long as your function}\par
