08454             {\cf20 // NB- if you have thousands of entries this approach may be too inefficient and may require user-side clipping}\par
08455             {\cf20 // to only process visible items. The clipper will automatically measure the height of your first item and then}\par
08456             {\cf20 // "seek" to display only items in the visible area.}\par
08457             {\cf20 // To use the clipper we can replace your standard loop:}\par
08458             {\cf20 //      for (int i = 0; i < Items.Size; i++)}\par
08459             {\cf20 //   With:}\par
08460             {\cf20 //      ImGuiListClipper clipper;}\par
08461             {\cf20 //      clipper.Begin(Items.Size);}\par
08462             {\cf20 //      while (clipper.Step())}\par
08463             {\cf20 //         for (int i = clipper.DisplayStart; i < clipper.DisplayEnd; i++)}\par
08464             {\cf20 // - That your items are evenly spaced (same height)}\par
08465             {\cf20 // - That you have cheap random access to your elements (you can access them given their index,}\par
08466             {\cf20 //   without processing all the ones before)}\par
08467             {\cf20 // You cannot this code as-is if a filter is active because it breaks the 'cheap random-access' property.}\par
08468             {\cf20 // We would need random-access on the post-filtered list.}\par
08469             {\cf20 // A typical application wanting coarse clipping and filtering may want to pre-compute an array of indices}\par
08470             {\cf20 // or offsets of items that passed the filtering test, recomputing this array when user changes the filter,}\par
08471             {\cf20 // and appending newly elements as they are inserted. This is left as a task to the user until we can manage}\par
08472             {\cf20 // to improve this example code!}\par
08473             {\cf20 // If your items are of variable height:}\par
08474             {\cf20 // - Split them into same height items would be simpler and facilitate random-seeking into your list.}\par
08475             {\cf20 // - Consider using manual call to IsRectVisible() and skipping extraneous decoration from your items.}\par
