09922     {\cf20 // [Optional] Notify the system of Tabs/Windows closure that happened outside the regular tab interface.}\par
09923     {\cf20 // If a tab has been closed programmatically (aka closed from another source such as the Checkbox() in the demo,}\par
09924     {\cf20 // as opposed to clicking on the regular tab closing button) and stops being submitted, it will take a frame for}\par
09925     {\cf20 // the tab bar to notice its absence. During this frame there will be a gap in the tab bar, and if the tab that has}\par
09926     {\cf20 // disappeared was the selected one, the tab bar will report no selected tab during the frame. This will effectively}\par
09927     {\cf20 // give the impression of a flicker for one frame.}\par
09928     {\cf20 // We call SetTabItemClosed() to manually notify the Tab Bar or Docking system of removed tabs to avoid this glitch.}\par
09929     {\cf20 // Note that this completely optional, and only affect tab bars with the ImGuiTabBarFlags_Reorderable flag.}\par
09930     {\cf18 void} NotifyOfDocumentsClosedElsewhere()\par
09931     \{\par
09932         {\cf19 for} (MyDocument& doc : Documents)\par
09933         \{\par
09934             {\cf19 if} (!doc.Open && doc.OpenPrev)\par
09935                 ImGui::SetTabItemClosed(doc.Name);\par
09936             doc.OpenPrev = doc.Open;\par
09937         \}\par
09938     \}\par
09939 \};\par
